---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../site.config.ts";

const description = `How ${site.name} collects, uses and protects your personal data.`;
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description={description} path="/privacy">
  <div class="wrap page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      This policy explains what personal data {site.name} collects, how it is
      used, and the choices and rights you have. It applies to this website only.
    </p>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: 19 October 2026</p>

    <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
    <p>
      {site.name} is an independent website about living and working remotely in
      Chiang Mai. For any privacy question, or to exercise your rights below,
      contact <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What is collected</h2>
    <p><strong>Analytics.</strong> This site uses Google Analytics to understand
      how visitors find and use it (such as pages viewed and approximate
      location). For visitors in the UK, EU and EEA, these analytics cookies are
      only set after consent is given through the cookie banner. Your consent
      choice is stored in your browser so you are not asked again.</p>
    <p><strong>Community story submissions.</strong> If you submit a story
      through the community form (powered by Tally), the information you provide
      is collected: your name, email address, your story, any photos, your
      website or social link, and the tags you choose. Submissions are stored in
      Google Drive for review.</p>
    <p><strong>Contact form.</strong> If you use the contact form (powered by
      Formspree), your name, email address and message are collected so your
      enquiry can be answered.</p>
    <p><strong>Email list.</strong> If you choose to join the mailing list, your
      email address is collected and stored with the email provider (MailerLite)
      so updates can be sent. You can unsubscribe at any time using the link in
      any email.</p>

    <h2>How your information is used</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To review and, with your consent, publish community stories.</li>
      <li>To reply to messages sent through the contact form.</li>
      <li>To send email updates, if you have subscribed.</li>
      <li>To measure and improve how the site performs (analytics).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Publishing community stories</h2>
    <p>
      When you submit a story, you are asking for it to be considered for
      publication. If it is published, your chosen story title, your name, your
      photos and a link to the website or social profile you provided will appear
      publicly on the site. Your email address is never published. If you would
      like a published story removed, contact
      <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Who your data is shared with</h2>
    <p>
      Personal data is only shared with the service providers that make this site
      work, each acting as a data processor: Google (analytics), Tally (story
      form), Formspree (contact form), MailerLite (email), Google Drive (storage)
      and Cloudflare (hosting and content delivery). Some of these providers are
      based outside the UK and EEA, which means your data may be transferred and
      processed abroad under appropriate safeguards. Their own privacy policies
      explain how they handle data:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://tally.so/help/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Tally</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Formspree</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.mailerlite.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MailerLite</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cloudflare</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p>Your data is never sold.</p>

    <h2>How long data is kept</h2>
    <p>
      Community submissions are kept for as long as the story remains published,
      or until you ask for it to be removed. Contact messages are kept only as
      long as needed to deal with your enquiry. Mailing list data is kept until
      you unsubscribe. Analytics data is retained according to Google Analytics'
      standard retention settings.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      If you are in the UK or EU, you have the right to access the personal data
      held about you, to have it corrected or deleted, to object to or restrict
      its use, and to withdraw consent at any time. To exercise any of these,
      email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. You also have the
      right to complain to the UK Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) at
      <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>,
      or your local data protection authority.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>This site is not directed at children, and does not knowingly collect data from anyone under 16.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      This policy may be updated from time to time. The date at the top of this
      page shows when it was last changed.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
